**The Problem: Over-permissive Lambda Role:**
```json
// BAD: Lambda can do EVERYTHING
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [{
    "Effect": "Allow",
    "Action": "*",
    "Resource": "*"
  }]
}
```

**The Fix: Least privilege role:**
```json
// GOOD: Lambda can only read from one specific S3 bucket
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::my-specific-bucket/input/*"
    },
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["dynamodb:PutItem"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:dynamodb:us-east-1:123456:table/ProcessedItems"
    },
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["logs:CreateLogGroup", "logs:CreateLogStream", "logs:PutLogEvents"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:logs:*:*:*"
    }
  ]
}
```

**AWS IAM Access Analyzer:**
```bash
# Find over-permissive Lambda roles
aws iam list-roles --query 'Roles[?contains(RoleName, `lambda`)]'
aws iam get-role-policy --role-name MyLambdaRole --policy-name MyPolicy

# Check what a role actually accesses (Access Advisor)
aws iam generate-service-last-accessed-details --arn arn:aws:iam::123456:role/MyLambdaRole
```
